<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16095" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕrechtheus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ), ei,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρεχθεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a fabled king of
				Athens</i>, <i>father of Procris</i>, <i>Orithyia</i>, <i>Chthonia</i>, <i>and Creüsa</i>, <i>who
				devoted themselves to death for their country</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Tusc. 1, 48, 116</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin.
				5, 22, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. N. D. 3, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Sest.
				21, 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6, 667 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7,
			697</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 2, 6,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕrechthēus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Erechthean</i>, and <b>poet.</b> for <i>Athenian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					5, 204</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					8, 548</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 6, 1, 1</span></i>
			
			<i>ext.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕrecthī-dae</span></b> ,
			ārum, m., <b>poet.</b>, <i>the Athenians</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				430</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕrechthis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>a
				daughter of Erechtheus</i>, <i>Orithyia</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. H.
			16</span></i>; <i>Procris</i>, <i><span class="en">id. M. 7,
				726</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
